    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="1893" n="1788" xml:id="pg1788"/>

                <head>501. Memorandum From Keeny to Kistiakowsky<anchor n="1" xml:id="d501-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-10-15">October 15,
                        1959</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d501-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d501-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Suggested Course of Action for U.S. Delegation in Nuclear Test
                        Negotiations</item>
                </list>
                <p>Attached is a copy of the instructions for the U.S. Delegation to the forthcoming
                    continuation of the Nuclear Test Negotiations as approved by Dillon and a copy
                    of a letter from Gates to Dillon commenting on these instructions. Dillon has
                    informed Gates that his suggested change in the “objective” will not be
                    incorporated in the instructions. I learned privately that the original letter
                    from Defense as prepared by Irwin was considerably stronger and that Gates has
                    toned it down before signing.</p>
                <p>With regard to the instructions, I consider them acceptable in view of present
                    policy decision. However, the delegation can probably count on some real trouble
                    since it cannot state any quota that would be acceptable to U.S. If pressed on
                    this by Soviets as it probably will be, the Delegation will have problem in
                    maintaining illusion that we would accept comprehensive treaty if Soviets were
                    only reasonable on inspections.</p>


                <xi:include href="d501-a1.xml" xpointer="d501-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
